{
  "dom_id": "step-e3597",
  "name": "Example: Finding the Intervals on Which a Radical Function Is Continuous",
  "problem": "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{4-x}$ is continuous.",
  "worked_solution": "Our function is a radical function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\sqrt{4-x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n4-x\\geq 0\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad \nx\\leq 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $(-\\infty,4]$, and the function is continuous on this interval.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
